  - id: the_love_oracle
    displayName: The Love Oracle
    flavorText: Answers Israel's doubt of God's love by declaring 'Jacob have I loved,
      but Esau have I hated,' contrasting Israel's preserved heritage against Edom's
      laid-waste mountains.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Opens the book by answering Israel's doubt of God's love by contrasting
      the LORD's covenant choice of Jacob (Israel) against Esau (Edom), whose land
      the text says was laid waste, reassuring a discouraged post-exilic community
      of God's continued covenant love toward the nation.
    deliveredByManagerId: malachi
    managerId: jacob_have_i_loved
