  - id: the_prophets_promise
    displayName: The Prophet's Promise
    flavorText: Closes the Old Testament with the promise that the LORD will send
      Elijah the prophet before the great and dreadful day of the LORD, to turn the
      hearts of fathers to children and children to fathers.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Closes the book -- and the Protestant Old Testament as a whole -- with
      a charge to remember the law of Moses and a promise that the LORD will send
      Elijah the prophet before the great and dreadful day of the LORD, who will
      turn the heart of the fathers to the children and the children to their fathers
      so the land is not struck with a curse.
    deliveredByManagerId: malachi
